The mobile application must remain responsive on ordinary devices and mobile networks.

Prioritise:

- Fast initial rendering.
- Efficient API requests.
- Lazy loading of less frequently used screens.
- Lightweight charts.
- Minimal unnecessary re-renders.
- Reasonable image and asset sizes.
- Efficient list rendering.
- Stable scrolling.
- Responsive form interactions.
- Clear loading feedback.

Do not load every financial module and historical dataset on the Home screen.

Load additional details when users navigate to the relevant module.

Use skeleton loaders only when they improve perceived performance.

Avoid large animations that make financial screens feel slow.

