# 18. Error, Empty, and Loading States

Every major screen and financial operation must have intentional states.

## Loading

Show a useful loading indicator or skeleton without making the application appear frozen.

## Empty data

Explain what the user can add and why it matters.

## Incomplete profile

Show available data and identify missing information.

## Network failure

Provide a clear message and a retry option where appropriate.

## Validation failure

Identify the field or input that needs correction.

## Authentication failure

Use the existing session-expiration and reauthentication flow.

## AI failure

Preserve the user's message, explain that the advisor could not complete the request, and offer a retry where appropriate.

## Stale financial data

Show the last-updated information when available.

Do not silently replace missing API responses with fabricated values or misleading zeroes.

A genuine zero balance must remain distinguishable from an unknown balance.

